# Every text file is LF in the working tree, Windows checkouts included: the
# files are read by Linux containers (configs, scripts, env examples), and a
# stray CR breaks them in ways that are hard to see.
* text=auto eol=lf
# Shell scripts must keep LF endings even on Windows checkouts, or the Linux build
# container fails with "./gradlew: not found" (the shebang ends in \r).
gradlew text eol=lf
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.bat   text eol=crlf
*.jar   binary
*.sql   text eol=lf
*.conf  text eol=lf
*.ttf   binary
